diff --git a/.changeset/consumer-upgrade-process-detail.md b/.changeset/consumer-upgrade-process-detail.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..e1d0469f3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/consumer-upgrade-process-detail.md
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+---
+"@agent-teams/docs-protocol-agent-teams": patch
+---
+
+Report the tail of both output streams, labelled, when a consumer upgrade process
+fails. pnpm writes `ERR_PNPM_*` to stdout and configuration warnings to stderr, so
+a consumer with an unset variable in its user npmrc used to see only the warning.
diff --git a/.changeset/feature-module-standard-kernel.md b/.changeset/feature-module-standard-kernel.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..fa787bcb2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/feature-module-standard-kernel.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+---
+"@agent-teams/feature-module-standard": minor
+---
+
+Add the opt-in Feature Module Standard package: a pure kernel that checks the
+declared structure of one production module (feature tree and sub-features,
+visibility, edge classes, composition contracts, republication, layer direction,
+cycles, test ownership and growth metrics) and the shared conformance fixtures
+that every adopting checker runs. Repository policy stays input; the kernel
+reads no files and widens no rule.
diff --git a/.changeset/findings-baseline-source-graph.md b/.changeset/findings-baseline-source-graph.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..2e98689b3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/findings-baseline-source-graph.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+---
+"@agent-teams/engineering-foundation": minor
+---
+
+Add the architecture-neutral core mechanisms: a shrink-only findings baseline
+(`baseline check`, `init` and `prune` commands for Oxlint findings, and pure
+functions on `@agent-teams/engineering-foundation/ratchet`), growth budgets that
+only warn, and a public source graph with strongly connected components on
+`@agent-teams/engineering-foundation/source-graph`. `quality.source-coverage`
+also reads Feature Module Standard v1.1 production mappings; its topology and
+all existing diagnostics are unchanged.
diff --git a/.changeset/public-api-git-timeout.md b/.changeset/public-api-git-timeout.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..9393586aa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/public-api-git-timeout.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+---
+"@agent-teams/engineering-foundation": patch
+---
+
+Give the git calls that read repository identity in `package.public-api-compatibility`
+a 60 second deadline instead of 10 seconds. A cold Windows runner could exceed ten
+seconds and fail with `UNEXPECTED_PROCESS_FAILURE`. On Windows the deadline also covers
+the Job Object wrapper (the PowerShell bootstrap with its `Add-Type` C# compilation and the
+Node process host), not only git.
diff --git a/.changeset/source-graph-runtime-facts.md b/.changeset/source-graph-runtime-facts.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..a568479af
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/source-graph-runtime-facts.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+---
+"@agent-teams/engineering-foundation": minor
+---
+
+Preserve reference kinds and unresolved computed loaders in the public source
+graph. Observe direct ESM runtime export names and kinds through the existing
+Oxc parser, with per-file coverage and explicit unsupported forms instead of
+fabricated complete counts. Keep unresolved, external and parse-failure lanes.
+
+Consumers retain ownership of syntax restrictions and CMS/FMS profile mappings.
+This additive source API changes no dependency-policy schema, architecture
+standard, consumer pin or release admission.
